TITLE:: HPTransformerStudio
SUMMARY:: Classic Musical RT 8D Studio with harmonized presets, Live Concert, and Stage Mode
CATEGORIES:: Libraries>HPTransformer, GUI, Machine Learning
RELATED:: Classes/HPtransformerRT

DESCRIPTION::
HPTransformerStudio V8.7.3 controls the HPtransformerRT V30.3.0 Classic Musical RT engine. This edition uses preset names consistent with the Classic engine, adds the Classic Live Concert preset, and retains Stage Mode for suspending periodic display updates.

The Studio includes a Dashboard, runtime controls, manual parameters, morphing, generation, memory, surprise, OSC, ControlBus, complete configuration sets, graphs, heatmaps, presets, sessions, RCU, and logs. It does not include an Advanced RT page.

The OSC worker runs at 20 Hz, Learn/N defaults to 8, and the visual refresh interval is 0.75 seconds.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a Studio associated with an engine.

ARGUMENT:: transformer
An HPtransformerRT instance. If nil, the Studio creates a default 8 x 8 engine.

ARGUMENT:: externalTransformerKey
The Symbol naming the external variable to synchronize. The default value is code::\hpTR::.

RETURNS::
An HPTransformerStudio instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: front
Builds the window if necessary and brings it to the front.

RETURNS::
The Studio.

METHOD:: close
Closes the window and its associated routines.

RETURNS::
The Studio.

METHOD:: transformer
Returns the active engine.

RETURNS::
An HPtransformerRT instance.

METHOD:: externalTransformerKey
Returns the external synchronization key.

RETURNS::
A Symbol.

METHOD:: attachControlBus
Attaches a control bus. Use 8 channels for the default profile.

ARGUMENT:: bus
The Bus.control used for the outputs.

RETURNS::
The Studio.

METHOD:: detachControlBus
Detaches the control bus.

RETURNS::
The Studio.

SECTION:: Creating the Studio

CODE::
(
~hpTR = HPtransformerRT.new;
~studio = HPTransformerStudio.new(~hpTR, \hpTR).front;
)
::

SECTION:: General Classic presets

LIST::
## Classic - Cautious: slow learning, strong protection, moderate replay, and low exploration.
## Classic - Balanced: general-purpose balance between adaptation, memory, and generation.
## Classic - Reactive: faster learning, short context, and more responsive generation.
## Classic - Light Continuity: continuity produced by conventional memory and trajectory mechanisms, without additional temporal smoothing.
## Classic - Maximum Stability: slow learning, bounded gradients, stronger protection, and increased replay.
## Classic Musical Direct: lightweight musical baseline, 20 Hz, Learn/N = 8, with RCU and Details disabled.
## Classic Live Concert: stage-oriented balance, 20 Hz, Learn/N = 6, with learning and generation enabled.
## Classic Generation Only: external learning disabled, 20 Hz, Learn/N = 16.
## Classic Ultra CPU - Fast Learning: minimal load, strong adaptation, 20 Hz, and Learn/N = 4.
::

SECTION:: Classic Live Concert

The Live Concert preset applies moderate learning, low replay, one memory recall, one trajectory recall, a generation window of 4, and moderate variation.

CODE::
learningRate = 0.00030
replayRate = 0.03
memoryRecallSize = 1
trajectoryRecallSize = 1
generationWindowSize = 4
attentionTemperature = 1.10
deltaScale = 0.34
trajectoryExplorationGain = 0.004
::

Operational preset settings:

LIST::
## OSC processing: 20 Hz.
## Learn/N: 6.
## Learning: ON.
## Generation: ON.
## OSC Details: OFF.
## RCU: OFF.
::

SECTION:: Complete Classic configurations

LIST::
## Classic Cautious: 8D tracking that remains close to the gesture, with restrained generation.
## Classic Balanced: general-purpose balance with output-specific tracking.
## Classic Expressive: higher temperature and low tracking.
## Classic Installation: slow learning, strong protection, and cautious generation.
::

SECTION:: Stage Mode

The Dashboard button toggles between Control Mode and Stage Mode.

LIST::
## Control Mode: diagnostics, graphs, heatmaps, logs, and indicators are updated.
## Stage Mode: the periodic refresh routine is suspended and OSC Details is forced OFF.
## OSC, the worker, learnEvent, generateStep, network output, and ControlBus continue to operate.
## Returning to Control Mode triggers a single refresh.
::

NOTE::
Stage Mode reduces GUI load, but does not reduce the internal cost of learnEvent. To reduce that cost, increase Learn/N or lower the processing rate in Hz.
::

SECTION:: Direct tracking by dimension

Direct tracking is applied after generateStep in the Studio's OSC processing chain.

CODE::
output[i] = (output[i] * (1.0 - mix[i])) + (input[i] * mix[i]);
::

Lightweight 8D example for live performance:

CODE::
0.12,0.06,0.03,0.12,0.06,0.03,0.12,0.06
::

To evaluate the raw engine output, use a global tracking value of 0 or eight zero values.

SECTION:: 8D OSC

With the default profile, the input path expects exactly eight values.

CODE::
n = NetAddr("127.0.0.1", 57120);
n.sendMsg("/hptransformer/input", 0.20,0.40,0.70,0.50,0.30,0.80,0.60,0.10);
::

SECTION:: 8D ControlBus

CODE::
~bus = Bus.control(s, 8);
~studio.attachControlBus(~bus);
::

SECTION:: Live-performance strategy

NUMBEREDLIST::
## Create a new engine.
## Apply Classic Live Concert.
## Start with Direct Tracking = 0.
## Confirm 20 Hz, Learn/N = 6, and Details OFF.
## Enable Stage Mode after completing the setup.
## If CPU usage is too high, switch to 15 Hz and Learn/N = 8.
## If adaptation is too slow, try Learn/N = 4 or 2.
::

SECTION:: Sessions

Sessions save the engine, runtime parameters, RCU state, OSC settings, direct-tracking values, graphs, and logs. After loading, the configured external variable is reassigned to the restored engine.

SECTION:: Verification after loading

CODE::
[
    \key, ~studio.externalTransformerKey,
    \sameObject, ~hpTR === ~studio.transformer
].postln;
::
